<%#
  One view, both outcomes. A redirect with a flash message would be the usual
  shape, but flash is stored in the session — and issuing a session cookie is
  the thing these public pages go out of their way not to do.

  subscriber is nil when the honeypot was filled: a bot gets the same page a
  person does, and learns nothing.
%>
<% failed = subscriber&.errors&.any? %>

<% content_for :title, failed ? "That address didn't look right — Remindly" : "You're on the list — Remindly" %>

<% if failed %>
  <h1>That address didn't look right</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    <%= subscriber.errors.full_messages.to_sentence %>. Have another go — or
    just email <a href="mailto:hello@remindly.care">hello@remindly.care</a> and
    I'll add you by hand.
  </p>

  <%= render "shared/subscribe_form", source: "retry" %>
<% else %>
  <h1>You're on the list</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    The routine sheet is on its way to your inbox. If it hasn't arrived in a few
    minutes, check the spam folder — and if it isn't there either, email
    <a href="mailto:hello@remindly.care">hello@remindly.care</a> and I'll sort it out.
  </p>

  <p>
    You can print the sheet right now without waiting:
    <a href="<%= routine_sheet_path %>">open the daily routine sheet</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= login_path %>">Try Remindly — it's free</a>
    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="<%= blog_path %>">Read something first</a>
  </div>
<% end %>
